Lens profiles plug-in for Lumen 1.0
===================================

Gives Lumen's Lens Correction group (in the Adjustments tab, Lumen 0.0.38
and later) the profiles of 1,533 lenses: how each bends straight lines
(distortion), fringes edges with colour towards the corners (lateral
chromatic aberration) and darkens the corners (vignetting), as measured
by the lensfun project. Lumen undoes them for the photo's focal length
and aperture, as much as you choose.

Auto finds the photo's lens from what the camera wrote in the file (the
lens's name, or its focal lengths and aperture, and the camera, which
says which lenses fit it). When it can't tell, choose the lens from the
Lens menu: the likeliest first, then every one that fits by maker. If
the camera isn't in the database, the Camera link chooses one like it
(the same mount, the nearest sensor size), so the profile is scaled for
the right size of sensor.

The profile is kept with the photo's adjustments, so the photo looks the
same with or without the plug-in (and with a newer one). Without it,
Lumen's Lens Correction group still has Manual, which corrects barrel
or pincushion distortion by hand.

It is only data: a text file, Lenses, which Lumen reads itself. It lives
in Lumen's Plugins directory (!Lumen.Plugins.Lens); PackMan puts it
there. Lumen finds it the next time it starts.

The LumenLens User Guide is in Guide, beside this ReadMe: open
Guide.index/html in a web browser.

The lens database is the lensfun project's (https://lensfun.github.io),
by its contributors, under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
3.0 licence (see Licence): Lenses is the same facts in a smaller form,
made by Lumen's tools/lensdb.py, and shared under the same licence.
Lumen's own code reads it (none of lensfun's library is used). The
plug-in's description and ReadMe are copyright (C) 2026 Andrew Youll.
